1
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:46,800
Survival is no game

2
00:07:21,600 --> 00:07:27,600
Tekken is a crime, drama, action film directed by Dwight H. Little.

3
00:11:02,400 --> 00:11:08,400
In the year of 2039, after World Wars destroy much of the civilization as we know it, territories are no
longer run by governments, but by corporations; the mightiest of which is the Mishima Zaibatsu.

4
00:14:43,200 --> 00:14:49,200
In order to placate the seething masses of this dystopia, Mishima sponsors Tekken, a
tournament in which fighters battle until only one is left standing.

5
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:30,000
Jin Kazama, played by Jonathan Patrick Foo.

6
00:22:04,800 --> 00:22:10,800
Christie Monteiro, played by Kelly Overton.

7
00:25:45,600 --> 00:25:51,600
Heihachi Mishima, played by Cary-Hiroyuki Tagawa.

8
00:29:26,400 --> 00:29:32,400
Kazuya, played by Ian Anthony Dale.

9
00:33:07,200 --> 00:33:13,200
Steve Fox, played by Luke Goss.

10
00:36:48,000 --> 00:36:54,000
Eddy Gordo, played by Lateef Crowder.

11
00:40:28,800 --> 00:40:34,800
Tekken is a 2009 American science fiction martial arts film loosely based on the video game
series of the same name developed and published by Namco / Bandai Games, Inc.

12
00:44:09,600 --> 00:44:15,600
It was directed by Dwight Little from a screenplay by Alan B.

13
00:47:50,400 --> 00:47:56,400
The film stars Jon Foo, Kelly Overton, Cary-Hiroyuki Tagawa, Ian Anthony Dale,
Cung Le, Darrin Dewitt Henson, Candice Hillebrand, and Luke Goss.

14
00:51:31,200 --> 00:51:37,200
The plot follows Jin Kazama in his attempts to enter the Iron Fist Tournament in order to avenge the loss of his
mother, Jun Kazama, by confronting the forces of the city that are also holding the competition.

15
00:55:12,000 --> 00:55:18,000
The film was originally announced by publisher Namco / Bandai in
2002, but did not start development until 2007.

16
00:58:52,800 --> 00:58:58,800
Experienced in sports movies, Little decided to make Tekken focused on realism, resulting in the removal
of supernatural elements from the video game series as well as comic relief characters.

17
01:02:33,600 --> 01:02:39,600
This also led to the inclusion of martial artists as the main
cast to produce well-choreographed battles.

18
01:06:14,400 --> 01:06:20,400
Tekken premiered at the American Film Market on November 5, 2009, and was released
direct-to-video in the United States on July 19, 2011, by Anchor Bay Entertainment.

19
01:09:55,199 --> 01:10:01,199
The film bombed at the box office with a gross of $1.6 million worldwide.

20
01:13:36,000 --> 01:13:42,000
Critical reception was unfavorable, with the film generally praised for its fighting scenes, but
criticized for its unfaithful narrative and poor acting within the main cast.

21
01:17:16,800 --> 01:17:22,800
The criticism also came from the video game series'
executive director Katsuhiro Harada.

22
01:20:57,600 --> 01:21:03,600
Nevertheless, Tekken spawned the 2014 prequel Tekken 2: Kazuya's Revenge.

23
01:24:38,400 --> 01:24:44,400
The film explores themes of martial arts, dystopia, based on
video game, martial arts tournament, 2030s.

24
01:28:19,200 --> 01:28:25,200
The tone is emotional and thought_provoking and intense.
